# Copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust locally.
#
# Per CONFIGURATION.md: this file holds *values* only (ports, bootstrap
# servers, topic names, credentials, replica counts, image/build-context
# selection). Structural choices (a dev's own Avro schema directory, a dev's
# own service source) are volume mounts / build-context swaps, not env vars -
# see CONFIGURATION.md for why that split is deliberate.
#
# Real entries below were first meant to arrive in M1, but nothing actually
# consumed them until M2's order-service Kafka producer - added here now that
# there's a real reader for them.
#
# NOTE: docker-compose auto-loads this file for variable substitution inside
# compose files, but a locally-run Spring Boot process (`mvn spring-boot:run`)
# does NOT read .env automatically - order-service's application.yml uses
# ${VAR:default} placeholders that only see real OS/shell environment
# variables. The defaults below already match docker-compose.base.yml's
# published ports, so order-service works out of the box without exporting
# anything; only export these yourself if you need to override a default
# (e.g. pointing at a different Kafka cluster).

# Kafka broker's EXTERNAL listener, published by docker-compose.base.yml
KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092

# Schema Registry's REST API, published by docker-compose.base.yml
SCHEMA_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:8081

# Topic order-service publishes OrderCreated events to (see M1's schema work)
ORDER_EVENTS_TOPIC=order-events